    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d494">

                <pb facs="0947" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg823"/>

                <head>No. 490.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Señor Navarro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your two notes of the 28th of
                    August and 18th of October last, concerning the complaint of your government in
                    regard to <pb facs="0948" n="824" xml:id="pg824"/> the acts of a band headed by
                    one Robert E. Martin, I have the honor and pleasure of informing you that the
                    Secretary of the Interior, under date of the 28th ultimo, advises this
                    Department that the governor of the Territory of Arizona has been instructed to
                    investigate the complaint so far as to the hiding place of Martin being within
                    that Territory, and that should he be found within that jurisdiction the
                    authorities there are to take such measures as may be within their power to
                    breakup any band of robbers led by him and to preserve peace upon the frontier
                    between the two countries.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
